							},
							"paragraphStyle" : {
								"__type" : "textStyle"
							},
							"string" : "The stone's Zinc HTTP classes (`ZnClient`, `ZnResponse`, `ZnUtils`, ...) are the frozen native ones in `ZincGlobals`, older than GT's.  Only `ZnUrl` exists twice: the native one in `ZincGlobals` and GT's in `Globals`.  `String>>asZnUrl` deliberately answers the native one, because the native `ZnClient` consumes it.  Fill API gaps in the native classes with extension method descriptors."
						},
						{
							"__type" : "textSnippet",
							"children" : {
								"__type" : "snippets",
								"items" : [ ]
							},
							"createEmail" : {
								"__type" : "email",
								"emailString" : "<unknown>"
							},
							"createTime" : {
								"__type" : "time",
								"time" : {
									"__type" : "dateAndTime",
									"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-11-17T10:02:41.023621+01:00"
								}
							},
							"editEmail" : {
								"__type" : "email",
								"emailString" : "<unknown>"
							},
							"editTime" : {
								"__type" : "time",
								"time" : {
									"__type" : "dateAndTime",
									"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-11-17T10:02:41.023621+01:00"
								}
							},
							"uid" : {
								"__type" : "uid",
								"uidString" : "x6EQIBIARx6y9o4+r2Z9tw=="
							},
							"paragraphStyle" : {
								"__type" : "textStyle"
							},
							"string" : "The native Zinc has no TLS stream; {{gtClass:GtGsSecureSocketStream}} provides one by upgrading the connected socket with `GsSecureSocket newClientFromGsSocket:`.  `GsSecureSocket class>>setCaCertLocation` silently turns verification off when it finds no CA bundle, so set the bundle explicitly and fail if it is missing, and call `setExpectedHost:` for host-name checks."
						},
						{
							"__type" : "textSnippet",
							"children" : {
								"__type" : "snippets",
								"items" : [ ]
							},
							"createEmail" : {
								"__type" : "email",
								"emailString" : "<unknown>"
							},
							"createTime" : {
								"__type" : "time",
								"time" : {
									"__type" : "dateAndTime",
									"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-11-17T10:02:41.024186+01:00"
								}
