							"uid" : {
								"__type" : "uid",
								"uidString" : "qdU7uZnlScudd4i1OwMivw=="
							},
							"paragraphStyle" : {
								"__type" : "textStyle"
							},
							"string" : "The stone has no `AsyncFuture` runtime.  Gt4LlmCore provides {{gtClass:GtLSynchronousFuture}} and {{gtClass:GtLSynchronousPromise}}, with `ExecBlock>>asAsyncFuture` and `asAsyncPromise` bridges: the future evaluates its block on `await`, and the execution configuration is ignored.  Code that sends `asAsyncFuture` / `await:` runs unchanged."
						},
						{
							"__type" : "textSnippet",
							"children" : {
								"__type" : "snippets",
								"items" : [ ]
							},
							"createEmail" : {
								"__type" : "email",
								"emailString" : "<unknown>"
							},
							"createTime" : {
								"__type" : "time",
								"time" : {
									"__type" : "dateAndTime",
									"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-11-17T10:02:41.026089+01:00"
								}
							},
							"editEmail" : {
								"__type" : "email",
								"emailString" : "<unknown>"
							},
							"editTime" : {
								"__type" : "time",
								"time" : {
									"__type" : "dateAndTime",
									"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-11-17T10:02:41.026089+01:00"
								}
							},
							"uid" : {
								"__type" : "uid",
								"uidString" : "Cem9MbE3S16QtIZn8Cmviw=="
							},
							"paragraphStyle" : {
								"__type" : "textStyle"
							},
							"string" : "An error raised inside an announcement handler ends up as a rejected promise, so an example that waits on a semaphore times out (60 s) instead of failing.  In GtLChat a nil `response` usually hides the real error in the reply's `finalMessage` (a `GtLErrorMessage` with its `exception`); look there first."
						}
					]
				},
